---
import { SITE } from "../constants";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <blockquote>{SITE.description}</blockquote>
  <p>
    This library is not meant to be an all-in-one solution, but rather a
    sensible starting point for new projects.
  </p>
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>One:</strong>
    This library is meant to fully embrace <em>cascading style sheets</em> instead
    of giving you a way around them. It styles semantic elements in a simple, consistent
    way, setting you up to be able to extend and/or override the defaults as your
    design requires.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Two:</strong> The fundamental philosophy of this project is to use ratios
    to setup consistent sizing and spacing. The default is to use the <em
      >golden ratio</em
    >, but through config you can set to other classic ratios.
  </p>
  <p>
    Importantly, as is the case with design, a system has been created then
    meaningful deviations have been embraced to fine-tune it to look and feel
    correct. Thus, you may notice that we don't 100% adhere to the selected
    ratio, but default to doing so.
  </p>
  <hr />
  <p>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/demo`} class="button"
      >See demo &rarr;</a
    >
  </p>
  <hr />
  <h2>Features</h2>
  <p>Limited utility classes for ease of use:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>.h<em>n</em></code> classes to mimic headings but without the semantic
      meaning.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Layout>
